  "problem": "Find the circulation $\u0393$ of the the airflow $F$ along $C.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\u0393=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The circulation $\u0393$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nFrom step 6, we can write this as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =x{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(2-0)(4-0) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
